Use a WinRM HTTPS PSSession on port 5986, then query the remote machine’s Local Computer Trusted Root store.

$s = New-PSSession -ComputerName SERVER01 -UseSSL

Then:

Invoke-Command -Session $s -ScriptBlock {
    Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\Root |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Subject -like "*DigiCert*" -or
            $_.Issuer -like "*DigiCert*"
        } |
        Select-Object Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotBefore, NotAfter
}

If you want a cleaner table:

Invoke-Command -Session $s -ScriptBlock {
    Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\Root |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Subject -like "*DigiCert*" -or
            $_.Issuer -like "*DigiCert*"
        } |
        Select-Object Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter
} | Format-Table -AutoSize

To also check DigiCert intermediate certificates, query LocalMachine\CA:

Invoke-Command -Session $s -ScriptBlock {
    Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\CA |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Subject -like "*DigiCert*" -or
            $_.Issuer -like "*DigiCert*"
        } |
        Select-Object Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter
} | Format-Table -AutoSize

For your troubleshooting, I’d check both stores together:

Invoke-Command -Session $s -ScriptBlock {

    Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\Root |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Subject -like "*DigiCert*" -or
            $_.Issuer -like "*DigiCert*"
        } |
        Select-Object @{N='Store';E={'Root'}}, Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter

    Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\CA |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Subject -like "*DigiCert*" -or
            $_.Issuer -like "*DigiCert*"
        } |
        Select-Object @{N='Store';E={'Intermediate'}}, Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter

} | Format-Table -AutoSize

When finished:

Remove-PSSession $s
